  "verbalization": "Vidalol B is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which is a complex natural compound, and SNU-387 is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Anolobine. All three of these compounds are linked to MIP, suggesting a common mechanism of action or a shared target. The evidence indicates that Vidalol B may interact with SNU-387, which in turn may interact with MIP through a series of molecular pathways. The final scores for the relationships suggest a plausible, though not definitive, connection between Vidalol B and MIP, supported by the sequential targeting of SNU-387 and its derivatives to MIP. The mechanism likely involves the inhibition or modulation of a biological process that is central to the function of MIP, though the exact nature of this process remains to be elucidated.",
